Phase 1 -- tracer/scope unit test (no HF model). Env: torch 2.13.0+cpu, transformers 5.14.1, py3.14.
Test: develop/phase1_tracer_test.py

RESULT: PASS (both parts), deterministic across 2 runs (114 ops part1, 49 ops part2).

Part 1 (general): op capture OK, depends_on acyclic, weight_shape attribution survives
  weight.t() view (TRIVIAL propagation), scope labels layers 0/1 + blocks self_attn/mlp,
  functional softmax captured at dispatch (not a module boundary).
Part 2 (MLA isolated): KV down->up compression path captured; kv_up transitively depends
  on kv_down; latent dim (16) < expanded kv dim (128); decoupled-rope aten.cat captured.

Findings (src is CORRECT for intended input; two initial failures were TEST bugs):
  - dependency tracking, weight-through-view attribution, functional-op capture all verified good.
  - scope.py _LAYER_RE requires `.layers.N.` with a leading dot. Works for real HF
    AutoModelForCausalLM (always nested under model./transformer.). Does NOT match GPT-2
    style `transformer.h.N` -> will need generalizing at Phase 10 (gpt2-xl). Logged to memory.
